      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Bronx in 1975 was a chaotic battleground where white flight had already emptied the suburbs, leaving the borough to be filled by a rising tide of Black and Puerto Rican families who were often met with hostility from the entrenched white power structure. While the wealthy enclaves like Riverdale remained pristine and gated, the struggling neighborhoods were visually defined by crumbling public housing projects, graffiti-covered streets, and a pervasive sense of urban decay that was often exaggerated by media narratives blaming the new residents. This stark visual divide reflected a deep social fracture where the economic struggles of the majority were ignored by a system designed to maintain white supremacy, creating an atmosphere of tension and segregation that still echoes today.",
